This project includes code from SK8V, https://github.com/becaring/SK8V,
Copyright 2026 becaring, Apache License 2.0:
- gta/skate-gta/src/ped_rig.rs: SK8V's retarget (skatev-runtime/src/ped.rs), ported.
- gta/skate-gta/src/win/pose_hook.rs: SK8V's pose hook (host/src/pose_hook.cpp), ported to Rust.
- gta/skate-gta/src/live/ (bounds.rs, clean.rs, grid.rs, level.rs, rails.rs, and locate.rs, a
  Rust port of host/src/physics_level.cpp); SK8V's live reader is adapted from Sol4ra's
  LS-Skate-LiveCollision.

The GTAxSkate-bin.zip release builds (SkateVLegacy.asi, SkateVRuntime.dll,
prepare-board-parts.py, _common.py) are SK8V, modified: published v0.5.4 uses
SK8V 1.1.8; the current development candidate uses SK8V 1.1.9 with GTAxSkate's additions
(keyboard and mouse, board shop, camera views, trainer tuning and stamina, map helpers, skate radio, gentle peds, vehicle shapes), built
from https://github.com/Manatros/SK8V (branch skatemods). The changed files say what was added.

The Skate engine core (skate-host) comes from the 2010 Rust Rewrite Mashup,
https://github.com/chasmlol/2010-rust-rewrite-mashup, Apache License 2.0. It is not included
in this repository's source; the release builds contain it compiled, as SK8V's own do.

No Skate 3, skate., GTA V or other retail assets are included.
